1
00:00:04,767 --> 00:00:11,767
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:32,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:34,767
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:41,033
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:43,733
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:45,133
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,267 --> 00:00:46,600
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:48,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,167
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,333 --> 00:00:53,367
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:55,333
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,533 --> 00:00:57,833
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:57,967 --> 00:01:00,300
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,967 --> 00:01:03,000
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,133 --> 00:01:06,333
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,233
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,067 --> 00:01:11,567
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:12,767
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:14,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,533 --> 00:01:22,600
<i>We're fighting against cops.
They implement the law.</i>

21
00:01:22,733 --> 00:01:25,233
<i>- Can you pay for a lawyer?
- Gabo can!</i>

22
00:01:25,367 --> 00:01:26,900
<i>Do I really need
to dress like this?</i>

23
00:01:27,033 --> 00:01:29,800
<i>You need to blend in
for the sake of your missions.</i>

24
00:01:29,933 --> 00:01:34,067
<i>It's made out of bulletproof
and fireproof materials.</i>

25
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:35,833
<i>Now that you're holding
the gun,</i>

26
00:01:35,967 --> 00:01:37,533
<i>you must know
your responsibility.</i>

27
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,500
<i>I will use this
for the greater good.</i>

28
00:01:39,633 --> 00:01:41,067
<i>It's a good thing
you're suspended.</i>

29
00:01:41,233 --> 00:01:43,267
<i>Otherwise, you would've been
caught in the ambush, too.</i>

30
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,967
<i> Just drop that case, okay?</i>

31
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:46,467
Is that what you do at the NLEA?

32
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:48,500
<i>When things get difficult,
you just drop the case?</i>

33
00:01:48,633 --> 00:01:50,333
<i>After all, you don't care
about us.</i>

34
00:01:50,467 --> 00:01:51,933
<i>So we don't care
about you either.</i>

35
00:01:52,067 --> 00:01:53,333
<i> Could I borrow some money?</i>

36
00:01:53,467 --> 00:01:55,267
The mission hasn't even started,
you're already asking for money.

37
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,233
<i>I helped a mother and child
who'd been robbed.</i>

38
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:58,533
<i>I took the mother
to the hospital.</i>

39
00:01:58,667 --> 00:02:01,133
<i>That's your strength, Gabo.
Your heart.</i>

40
00:02:01,267 --> 00:02:02,800
<i>Gabo's heart is
in the right place.</i>

41
00:02:02,933 --> 00:02:04,633
<i>No one will help
a fellow Filipino</i>

42
00:02:04,767 --> 00:02:06,067
<i> if we don't help each other.</i>

43
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:08,233
[ROOSTER CROWING]

44
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:16,933
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

45
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,567
Betchay.

46
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:26,733
Betchay, I first have to talk
with Gabo and Mameng.

47
00:02:26,867 --> 00:02:29,867
We need to talk
about this as one family.

48
00:02:34,533 --> 00:02:37,300
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

49
00:02:37,433 --> 00:02:38,433
Betchay.

50
00:02:39,733 --> 00:02:43,167
Betchay, we can't just accept
their money!

51
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:52,633
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

52
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,533
[WOOD CRASHING]

53
00:03:05,667 --> 00:03:06,700
What's happening?

54
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:08,867
What was that?
Where did it come from?

55
00:03:10,667 --> 00:03:13,567
What's happening
to our roof? Rudy!

56
00:03:15,967 --> 00:03:17,333
Rudy, watch out!

57
00:03:17,467 --> 00:03:20,500
Something might fall.
This fell from the roof!

58
00:03:23,033 --> 00:03:25,400
[LOUD THUD, RATTLING]

59
00:03:26,367 --> 00:03:27,567
Dante!

60
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:28,800
- Anton!
- [MAMENG] Oh, no!

61
00:03:28,933 --> 00:03:30,567
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

62
00:03:31,433 --> 00:03:32,300
Man!

63
00:03:32,433 --> 00:03:33,333
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN]

64
00:03:33,467 --> 00:03:34,833
I heard something.

65
00:03:34,967 --> 00:03:37,533
- Rudy, man.
- Could you check the roof?

66
00:03:37,667 --> 00:03:39,633
- [MAMENG] Look at this.
- What happened here?

67
00:03:39,767 --> 00:03:43,200
It suddenly fell!
I'm lucky it didn't hit me.

68
00:03:44,033 --> 00:03:45,533
- That's the ceiling.
- Oh, yeah.

69
00:03:45,667 --> 00:03:49,400
Oh no. Oh no! Oh no!

70
00:03:50,367 --> 00:03:52,200
Your roof's turned weak, Rudy.

71
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,300
You have to change it!

72
00:03:54,467 --> 00:03:56,733
That's why rain goes
into your house

73
00:03:56,867 --> 00:03:58,500
every time it rains.

74
00:03:59,467 --> 00:04:02,067
Can't we do something
about it for now?

75
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:07,967
It'll be dangerous, Rudy,
because, as you know...

76
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:09,833
It just storms all of a sudden.

77
00:04:09,967 --> 00:04:13,033
Who knows, a strong wind
may pass us.

78
00:04:13,167 --> 00:04:15,433
I'm sure
it'll fly your roof away!

79
00:04:15,567 --> 00:04:18,133
If you start fixing that,
there's no turning back.

80
00:04:18,267 --> 00:04:20,400
That'll cost a lot of money.

81
00:04:20,533 --> 00:04:23,733
Well, what if something bigger
falls from there?

82
00:04:23,867 --> 00:04:25,867
We're lucky
nothing dangerous fell.

83
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,967
What if we get into
an accident here at home?

84
00:04:29,133 --> 00:04:30,367
I didn't say anything.

85
00:04:31,133 --> 00:04:32,200
If you have the money...

86
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,133
...then go.

87
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,333
Rudy, why don't
you just tell Gabo,

88
00:04:38,467 --> 00:04:40,167
so you can finally change
your roof?

89
00:04:41,233 --> 00:04:43,467
I'll tell him
when he gets home.

90
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,233
Alright, Rudy. Just call
on me and Badong

91
00:04:45,367 --> 00:04:47,733
once the materials arrive.

92
00:04:47,867 --> 00:04:49,167
- Thank you. Thank you.
- [ELTON] We'll handle it.

93
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:50,567
- [MAMENG] Thank you.
- [ELTON] Alright.

94
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:52,033
- Thank you!
- [RUDY] Thank you.

95
00:04:52,167 --> 00:04:53,633
- [BADONG] We'll get going.
- [MAMENG] Alright, thank you.

96
00:04:53,767 --> 00:04:55,900
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

97
00:04:57,567 --> 00:04:58,467
[GLASS THUDS]

98
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:02,433
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

99
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:05,833
Rudy, what will we do?
Will we change the roof?

100
00:05:05,967 --> 00:05:08,200
I think we should just
do something about it.

101
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:10,400
Is that so?
What about that person?

102
00:05:10,533 --> 00:05:12,233
What will you do with her?

103
00:05:12,367 --> 00:05:15,133
She's been ignoring us
ever since she didn't get

104
00:05:15,267 --> 00:05:17,767
what she wanted
with the settlement.

105
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:19,800
[DANTE] Yeah, I noticed it, too.

106
00:05:19,933 --> 00:05:25,767
It seems Betchay really wants
to get the settlement money.

107
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:28,100
But, you know, I was thinking...

108
00:05:28,667 --> 00:05:31,167
Why aren't they giving up?

109
00:05:31,833 --> 00:05:34,833
What if they really are
not cops?

110
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,933
[DANTE] I think
they're Jacinto's people,

111
00:05:37,067 --> 00:05:38,800
the owner of the land.

112
00:05:38,933 --> 00:05:41,700
You know what?
That's not impossible!

113
00:05:41,833 --> 00:05:46,567
Rudy, why don't we just
tell Gabo when he arrives?

114
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:48,200
So we can be ready!

115
00:05:49,733 --> 00:05:51,767
[DANTE] She's right.

116
00:05:51,900 --> 00:05:55,800
You should tell him
about the roof, too.

117
00:05:55,933 --> 00:05:59,167
Ask Gabo if he has
some extra money.

118
00:06:03,067 --> 00:06:06,633
Until the end, Gabo proved

119
00:06:06,767 --> 00:06:09,933
that you made the right decision
to recruit him, Pops.

120
00:06:10,533 --> 00:06:13,300
With everything
we asked him to do...

121
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:18,167
He didn't forget
help was waiting for him.

122
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:21,700
Lawin. Uwak.

123
00:06:22,733 --> 00:06:26,500
You have to accept Gabo
as a member of Anino.

124
00:06:26,633 --> 00:06:31,767
After all, over and over again,
he proved he has integrity!

125
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:39,533
Integrity, intelligence,
capability...

126
00:06:40,167 --> 00:06:43,433
...and a heart that beats
for others.

127
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:48,167
Those will be the keys
for Gabo to succeed

128
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:50,200
in his next missions.

129
00:06:50,833 --> 00:06:56,333
He will start the change
we have long been waiting for.

130
00:06:58,833 --> 00:07:00,400
Gabo is the fire...

131
00:07:01,033 --> 00:07:04,233
...that will burn
for the salvation of the masses.

132
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:06,467
Cheers.

133
00:07:19,467 --> 00:07:21,133
- How is she?
- Oh.

134
00:07:21,267 --> 00:07:23,233
Patchoy, wake up.

135
00:07:23,367 --> 00:07:26,300
- How is his mother?
- Well, um...

136
00:07:26,433 --> 00:07:28,667
They're currently operating
on her.

137
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:33,233
Um, but we don't have enough
money to pay for her fees.

138
00:07:36,367 --> 00:07:39,467
Don't worry.
I have money.

139
00:07:42,467 --> 00:07:43,433
Here.

140
00:07:44,167 --> 00:07:45,333
That's 100 thousand pesos.

141
00:07:45,467 --> 00:07:47,533
You can use it
to pay for the hospital fees.

142
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:48,700
Oh my.

143
00:07:49,833 --> 00:07:51,700
Thank you so, so much.

144
00:07:52,867 --> 00:07:53,867
Patchoy...

145
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:57,100
I'm sorry, but what's your name?

146
00:07:57,233 --> 00:07:59,133
- I didn't get it before.
- It's Gabo.

147
00:07:59,933 --> 00:08:01,867
- My name is Gabo.
- Gabo.

148
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:04,400
Thank you very much, Gabo.

149
00:08:05,367 --> 00:08:10,100
Um, I have to pay the fees now.
Could I leave Patchoy with you?

150
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:13,133
I'll look after him.

151
00:08:13,833 --> 00:08:16,367
Patchoy, I'll leave you
with Gabo, okay?

152
00:08:17,633 --> 00:08:18,633
Thank you.

153
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:20,900
[WOMAN EXHALES]

154
00:08:31,833 --> 00:08:34,467
- How are you?
- I'm doing fine.

155
00:08:36,767 --> 00:08:38,100
How's your mom?

156
00:08:38,233 --> 00:08:41,567
My aunt said the doctors
are operating on her.

157
00:08:44,633 --> 00:08:45,600
[GABO INHALES]

158
00:08:46,233 --> 00:08:47,233
Patchoy.

159
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:48,933
Don't worry.

160
00:08:50,933 --> 00:08:53,000
God will not abandon
your mother.

161
00:08:54,033 --> 00:08:56,000
I'm sure she'll survive.

162
00:08:56,933 --> 00:09:00,333
- I'm scared.
- Don't be afraid.

163
00:09:01,667 --> 00:09:04,033
You know, in our life...

164
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:10,967
We'll reach a point
where we have to be alone.

165
00:09:11,633 --> 00:09:14,767
You'll need to face it,
and fight against it.

166
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:18,567
[PATCHOY CRYING SOFTLY]

167
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:20,700
Don't cry, Patchoy.

168
00:09:21,833 --> 00:09:22,733
[PATCHOY SNIFFLES]

169
00:09:22,867 --> 00:09:25,000
I'm here for you.
I won't leave you alone.

170
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,967
[CRYING] Gabo...

171
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:37,100
[PATCHOY CRYING]

172
00:09:42,333 --> 00:09:45,567
It can't be bad news all day.

173
00:09:46,533 --> 00:09:48,000
Let's just trust that

174
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,400
the Internal Affairs decision
will work in our favor.

175
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,133
[SEQIOA] But wait, Karen.

176
00:09:53,133 --> 00:09:55,600
We're like sitting ducks.

177
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:58,000
First, we couldn't do anything
about what happened

178
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,667
to Team Bravo.

179
00:09:59,667 --> 00:10:01,000
Second,

180
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,067
there's nothing we can do about
Internal Affairs' decision.

181
00:10:04,533 --> 00:10:05,767
Absolutely nothing.

182
00:10:05,767 --> 00:10:08,800
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:10:10,467 --> 00:10:11,933
Ma'am, where are you going?

184
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,633
I'm going home.

185
00:10:14,633 --> 00:10:16,867
I'm no use here anyway.
I'm suspended.

186
00:10:17,633 --> 00:10:20,300
I'll just wait for
Internal Affairs' decision.

187
00:10:20,833 --> 00:10:22,967
But I'll stop by
Sir Delgado's office first.

188
00:10:22,967 --> 00:10:24,433
I'll just say goodbye.

189
00:10:24,433 --> 00:10:25,733
Oh, Sam.

190
00:10:25,733 --> 00:10:27,333
Are you feeling better?

191
00:10:27,333 --> 00:10:29,133
Come on.
I'll take you to Dad.

192
00:10:30,667 --> 00:10:32,033
- Dad?
- M-mmh.

193
00:10:32,033 --> 00:10:33,267
What do you mean, Dad?

194
00:10:33,267 --> 00:10:34,933
Can you please not come
with me?

195
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:37,567
Fine. But I'll wait for your
answer tomorrow, okay?

196
00:10:37,567 --> 00:10:38,567
Sam...

197
00:10:39,967 --> 00:10:41,367
I'm expecting an answer.

198
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:46,333
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

199
00:10:46,333 --> 00:10:48,300
[RALLOS]
Sir, expecting an answer?

200
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:49,600
Is there a new development?

201
00:10:50,333 --> 00:10:53,400
The development
is that Sam and I

202
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:55,400
have developed a relationship.

203
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,833
Tomorrow, we're official.

204
00:10:56,833 --> 00:11:00,600
The day after tomorrow,
she'll be Mrs. Sam Tuazon.

205
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:02,600
Oh, sir! Congratulations!

206
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:04,367
- You're my idol.
- Thank you.

207
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,133
[MUSIC FADES]

208
00:11:06,133 --> 00:11:07,300
[KNOCKS]

209
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:10,267
- Sir?
- Oh. Yes?

210
00:11:11,667 --> 00:11:12,933
I'm heading home.

211
00:11:12,933 --> 00:11:15,000
I just wanted to say goodbye.

212
00:11:16,933 --> 00:11:18,200
Sit down, please.

213
00:11:19,633 --> 00:11:24,267
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

214
00:11:24,267 --> 00:11:27,000
Sir, I know what happened
to Team Bravo is upsetting.

215
00:11:27,633 --> 00:11:30,300
If you need anything from me,
just let me know.

216
00:11:32,333 --> 00:11:34,533
I just want you to be safe.

217
00:11:37,033 --> 00:11:38,333
Thank you, sir.

218
00:11:38,967 --> 00:11:42,733
How did your questioning
with Internal Affairs go?

219
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:44,433
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

220
00:11:44,433 --> 00:11:48,900
Well, they said Mr. Chan's
statement could help me.

221
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:50,767
It could be the key
to clearing my name.

222
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:52,767
But then this happened.

223
00:11:54,233 --> 00:11:55,467
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

224
00:11:57,533 --> 00:12:00,967
We're dealing with a
dangerous enemy.

225
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:04,800
They're powerful.

226
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:07,867
We don't know
what they'll do next.

227
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:10,700
Sam...

228
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:12,700
Be careful.

229
00:12:12,700 --> 00:12:15,800
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

230
00:12:15,833 --> 00:12:19,033
If you notice
anything suspicious,

231
00:12:20,533 --> 00:12:21,800
just call me.

232
00:12:26,633 --> 00:12:29,900
[MUSIC BECOMES OMINOUS]

233
00:12:30,467 --> 00:12:31,767
Boss.

234
00:12:31,767 --> 00:12:34,033
We're only going after
one woman.

235
00:12:34,033 --> 00:12:36,433
Boss, why do we have
so many weapons?

236
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,433
I'm going to prove to Dad

237
00:12:41,067 --> 00:12:43,767
that I can finish the job
he gave me.

238
00:12:44,567 --> 00:12:46,067
What's your plan, boss?

239
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:49,467
We'll wait for her
outside the NCIA.

240
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:52,100
Her car's a yellow Camaro.

241
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:55,800
Whether she's alone in the car
or has someone with her,

242
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:58,267
I'll make sure this is
her last trip.

243
00:12:59,133 --> 00:13:00,167
Then let's go.

244
00:13:01,333 --> 00:13:04,700
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:05,867
[MUSIC FADES]

246
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:14,800
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

247
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:17,567
Thank God.
You're safe now, Ma.

248
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:20,267
Oh, Linda,
I'm glad you're awake.

249
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:24,000
By the way, this is Gabo.

250
00:13:24,033 --> 00:13:27,300
He's the one who saved you and
Pochoy when you were robbed.

251
00:13:28,033 --> 00:13:31,900
He also helped pay
for your hospital bills.

252
00:13:35,833 --> 00:13:37,533
Thank you so much, Gabo.

253
00:13:38,133 --> 00:13:40,200
I owe you my life.

254
00:13:41,967 --> 00:13:43,367
No, ma'am.

255
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:46,167
I just did what was right.

256
00:13:46,800 --> 00:13:48,767
What's important
is that you're safe.

257
00:13:48,767 --> 00:13:52,267
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

258
00:13:52,267 --> 00:13:53,467
[SIGHS]

259
00:13:53,467 --> 00:13:55,867
Pochoy, I'm leaving now.

260
00:13:56,433 --> 00:13:58,167
- Get well soon.
- Thank you.

261
00:13:59,133 --> 00:14:00,967
- Take care.
- Thank you.

262
00:14:01,633 --> 00:14:06,100
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

263
00:14:06,700 --> 00:14:07,867
[POCHOY] Mama...

264
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,167
Mama's okay now.

265
00:14:11,533 --> 00:14:14,200
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

266
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:17,267
<i> - I love you!
- I love you, Ma!</i>

267
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,567
[YOUNG GABO GIGGLING]

268
00:14:26,033 --> 00:14:28,633
[POCHOY CRYING]

269
00:14:28,667 --> 00:14:30,233
Mama's okay now.

270
00:14:35,433 --> 00:14:42,233
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

271
00:14:43,267 --> 00:14:44,533
Gabo!

272
00:14:49,367 --> 00:14:51,767
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

273
00:14:51,767 --> 00:14:53,433
Thank you, Gabo.

274
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:58,167
I hope someday,
I'll be able to help you, too.

275
00:14:58,667 --> 00:14:59,900
Don't worry.

276
00:14:59,900 --> 00:15:01,567
We'll see each other again.

277
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:03,267
Where do you live?

278
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:06,600
In Ginintuang Lupa,
over in Tondo.

279
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:12,500
I want to be like you
someday, Gabo.

280
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:14,500
Just be careful always, Pochoy.

281
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:16,000
Yes, Gabo.

282
00:15:18,500 --> 00:15:19,867
Okay, I'm heading out now.

283
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:31,567
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

284
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:52,633
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

285
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:03,067
[ENGINE REVVING]

286
00:16:06,567 --> 00:16:07,833
[PHONE RINGING]

287
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:11,200
She's left the NCIA.

288
00:16:11,900 --> 00:16:14,200
Boss, they said she's
already left the NCIA.

289
00:16:15,700 --> 00:16:16,767
This'll be easy.

290
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:20,100
Let's finish Samantha Jacinto
tonight.

291
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:21,967
[GUN COCKS]

292
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:27,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

293
00:16:27,633 --> 00:16:34,467
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

294
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:38,467
[IPE] Miss, I want it
grilled up good.

295
00:16:38,467 --> 00:16:39,533
[WOMAN] Sure thing.

296
00:16:39,533 --> 00:16:42,600
[INDISTINCT CHATTER
IN THE BACKGROUND]

297
00:16:42,633 --> 00:16:44,033
- Slather them with sauce.
- I thought that was Gabo.

298
00:16:44,033 --> 00:16:45,867
[BONG] Anything new here?
These look pretty old.

299
00:16:46,967 --> 00:16:48,900
- Are these about to expire?
- Hey, you guys.

300
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:50,933
Has Gabo reached out to you?

301
00:16:50,933 --> 00:16:52,200
Not yet.

302
00:16:52,200 --> 00:16:53,633
Oh no.

303
00:16:53,633 --> 00:16:56,133
What if something happened
to him?

304
00:16:56,133 --> 00:16:58,967
We were up against an armed
group last time, remember?

305
00:16:58,967 --> 00:17:00,500
A whole syndicate!

306
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:01,767
- So, what if--
- Tekla.

307
00:17:02,300 --> 00:17:04,133
It's like you don't know Gabo.

308
00:17:04,133 --> 00:17:07,433
He won't go down
no matter what you throw at him.

309
00:17:07,433 --> 00:17:09,400
Don't act like a stranger now.

310
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:11,967
Look, Ginintuang Lupa runs
through his veins.

311
00:17:11,967 --> 00:17:13,133
He's battle-hardened.

312
00:17:13,133 --> 00:17:14,767
Just because
he's battle-hardened

313
00:17:14,800 --> 00:17:16,467
doesn't mean
we shouldn't worry!

314
00:17:16,467 --> 00:17:18,833
We're not saying
you shouldn't worry.

315
00:17:18,833 --> 00:17:20,800
Honestly, we're worried too.

316
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:23,233
But we have to trust Gabo.

317
00:17:23,233 --> 00:17:24,300
[BONG] That's right.

318
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:26,133
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

319
00:17:26,133 --> 00:17:27,233
[IPE] Any updates, miss?

320
00:17:27,233 --> 00:17:28,733
Is it done? You've been
grilling it for ages.

321
00:17:28,733 --> 00:17:30,200
[BONG] It's not like you're
grilling dinosaur meat.

322
00:17:35,133 --> 00:17:36,200
[RUDY] Eat up.

323
00:17:37,433 --> 00:17:40,800
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]
- [UTENSILS SCRAPING]

324
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:41,767
Betchay.

325
00:17:42,633 --> 00:17:44,833
Join us for dinner
before you go.

326
00:17:47,333 --> 00:17:48,367
[UTENSILS THUD]

327
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:51,233
Babe...

328
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:54,100
What exactly is
your problem, Betchay?

329
00:17:55,100 --> 00:17:57,400
Just because the settlement
didn't go your way,

330
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,167
you want to act like a child?

331
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:03,667
Why are you insisting
on settling anyway?

332
00:18:03,667 --> 00:18:05,400
Maybe you already got something,

333
00:18:05,400 --> 00:18:07,000
that's why
you're acting like this.

334
00:18:07,667 --> 00:18:08,733
Besides,

335
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:11,467
it's possible that
they're working for Jacinto.

336
00:18:11,833 --> 00:18:14,067
Whether they're working
for Jacinto or the police,

337
00:18:14,067 --> 00:18:15,200
it doesn't matter.

338
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:19,200
They want to settle
because they did us wrong.

339
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:20,700
They want to help,

340
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,033
so I'll accept it.

341
00:18:22,067 --> 00:18:24,100
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

342
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,600
[TEKLA] Look, it's Gabo!
Save it for me.

343
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:26,867
- [TEKLA, BONG] Gabo!
- [ENGINE REVVING]

344
00:18:26,867 --> 00:18:28,000
Where have you been?

345
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,567
We were so worried about you.

346
00:18:29,567 --> 00:18:30,700
What took you so long?

347
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:32,967
[BONG] So, did they give you
a new mission?

348
00:18:35,467 --> 00:18:37,300
I underwent serious training.

349
00:18:39,800 --> 00:18:41,067
They made me sign,

350
00:18:41,933 --> 00:18:44,500
so I can't tell you what
my next missions will be about.

351
00:18:44,867 --> 00:18:47,633
Gabo, don't tell me they're
life-threatening or something.

352
00:18:47,633 --> 00:18:49,567
Because they made you sign
and all that.

353
00:18:49,567 --> 00:18:51,900
[BONG]
So what if they're dangerous?

354
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:53,500
We have nothing
to be afraid of, Tekla.

355
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:54,833
- We're strapped.
- [SCOFFS LIGHTLY]

356
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:56,333
Damn right, Gabo.

357
00:18:56,333 --> 00:18:58,900
If you need help, just say so.

358
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:00,567
We're ready
to back you up anytime.

359
00:19:00,567 --> 00:19:01,733
[GABO] Hey.

360
00:19:01,733 --> 00:19:03,067
Stop it, will you?

361
00:19:03,067 --> 00:19:05,100
Don't let those guns
make you cocky.

362
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:06,867
You might end up in a bad spot.

363
00:19:06,867 --> 00:19:08,133
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

364
00:19:08,133 --> 00:19:09,767
What happened to me...

365
00:19:09,767 --> 00:19:13,067
is the reason they haven't
continued their demolition here.

366
00:19:13,467 --> 00:19:14,500
[SCOFFS]

367
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:16,967
Are you going to betray us
just like that?

368
00:19:17,333 --> 00:19:18,567
[CHUCKLES DRYLY] Betray you?

369
00:19:18,567 --> 00:19:21,067
Aren't you being
a little harsh, Mameng?

370
00:19:21,067 --> 00:19:22,833
In case you forgot,

371
00:19:22,833 --> 00:19:26,333
all of us benefited
from what they gave us.

372
00:19:26,333 --> 00:19:29,700
Even the food you're eating now
was bought with their money.

373
00:19:29,733 --> 00:19:33,233
[DANTE] Betchay, money isn't
the issue here.

374
00:19:33,533 --> 00:19:38,500
The point is, you're putting
Ginintuang Lupa in danger.

375
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:42,733
[BETCHAY] Dante, Ginintuang Lupa
has always been in danger.

376
00:19:42,733 --> 00:19:44,767
This isn't our land!

377
00:19:44,767 --> 00:19:47,500
So as long as they want to give,

378
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,800
I'll accept it.

379
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:53,667
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

380
00:19:53,667 --> 00:19:54,667
[DOOR OPENS]

381
00:19:54,667 --> 00:19:55,933
[HEAVY FOOTSTEPS]

382
00:19:56,533 --> 00:19:58,233
- [TEKLA] Whoa, look at her.
- [BONG] Oh no...

383
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:02,067
[TEKLA] Hmph!

384
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:05,733
What made her
all worked up now?

385
00:20:06,467 --> 00:20:08,333
What else is new?
She's always angry.

386
00:20:08,533 --> 00:20:09,767
Just get used to it.

387
00:20:10,700 --> 00:20:12,367
- Go home, all of you.
- [ENGINE STARTS]

388
00:20:12,367 --> 00:20:13,833
[ENGINE ROARS]

389
00:20:13,833 --> 00:20:16,500
[ENGINE REVVING]

390
00:20:16,967 --> 00:20:17,900
[DOOR OPENS]

391
00:20:18,333 --> 00:20:19,500
[KNOCKS ON DOOR]

392
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:21,100
Sir?

393
00:20:24,467 --> 00:20:25,500
[DOOR CLOSES]

394
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:27,033
[CLEARING THROAT]

395
00:20:28,300 --> 00:20:29,267
Sir?

396
00:20:29,533 --> 00:20:31,000
I heard about what happened.

397
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:33,800
I've already informed
the families

398
00:20:33,800 --> 00:20:35,533
of Team Bravo what happened.

399
00:20:35,567 --> 00:20:36,700
[DELGADO INHALES DEEPLY]

400
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:41,133
They lost their loved ones
because of me.

401
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,000
Sir, please don't blame
yourself.

402
00:20:44,667 --> 00:20:47,433
I know it was well coordinated.

403
00:20:48,533 --> 00:20:49,833
The only question is,

404
00:20:52,267 --> 00:20:53,600
how...

405
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:59,500
...did the information about
transferring Mr. Chan leak out?

406
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,467
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

407
00:21:00,467 --> 00:21:02,967
I can't answer that right now.

408
00:21:03,433 --> 00:21:05,500
I'm still in a state
of confusion.

409
00:21:05,933 --> 00:21:07,033
[SCOFFS]

410
00:21:07,033 --> 00:21:10,967
Do you have any leads
or ideas as to who...

411
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,967
could have possibly leaked
the information?

412
00:21:12,967 --> 00:21:14,100
[DELGADO] Not yet.

413
00:21:14,100 --> 00:21:17,733
But I will get
to the bottom of this.

414
00:21:17,733 --> 00:21:21,667
It turns out the syndicate
does have a wide network.

415
00:21:21,667 --> 00:21:23,500
But I will
hold them accountable.

416
00:21:24,133 --> 00:21:25,167
Sir...

417
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:27,333
don't you think...

418
00:21:28,567 --> 00:21:30,633
...this fight is already
a lost cause?

419
00:21:32,433 --> 00:21:34,400
Maybe we should give up.

420
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:35,633
[DELGADO] Give up?

421
00:21:35,633 --> 00:21:39,800
Now that I've proven Sam
was right?

422
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:42,467
I could've crushed them
back then!

423
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:49,467
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

424
00:21:53,733 --> 00:21:55,200
- Guys.
- Any updates?

425
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:58,167
I got news about the ambush.

426
00:21:58,167 --> 00:22:01,033
They're already tracing
the vehicles used

427
00:22:01,033 --> 00:22:02,767
and running them
through the database.

428
00:22:02,767 --> 00:22:05,267
We need to get ahead
of the enemy's next move.

429
00:22:05,267 --> 00:22:08,133
We also need to know where
they're going next.

430
00:22:09,067 --> 00:22:10,700
By the way, where's Ma'am Sam?

431
00:22:11,167 --> 00:22:12,733
She already went home.

432
00:22:12,733 --> 00:22:13,767
What?

433
00:22:14,633 --> 00:22:16,067
You let her go home?

434
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:18,767
You know how dangerous
our situation is right now!

435
00:22:18,767 --> 00:22:20,667
Especially for Ma'am Sam!

436
00:22:20,667 --> 00:22:22,500
Come on, guys.

437
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:24,500
You have nothing to fear.

438
00:22:24,500 --> 00:22:25,833
It's Sam we're talking about.

439
00:22:25,833 --> 00:22:27,033
She's skilled.

440
00:22:27,433 --> 00:22:30,767
She can definitely
defend herself.

441
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:38,833
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [ENGINE REVVING]

442
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:41,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

443
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:42,267
There!

444
00:22:43,033 --> 00:22:44,467
[ENGINES START]

445
00:22:44,467 --> 00:22:46,467
[ENGINE REVVING]

446
00:22:46,467 --> 00:22:49,500
[TIRES SCREECHING]

447
00:22:49,533 --> 00:22:51,433
No way out for you, Samantha.

448
00:22:53,567 --> 00:22:54,633
[SEBASTIAN] Listen.

449
00:22:54,633 --> 00:22:56,733
If she ever gets into a fight,

450
00:22:56,733 --> 00:22:59,833
her opponents will be
the ones to suffer.

451
00:22:59,833 --> 00:23:02,267
Even if they trap her,
spray her with bullets,

452
00:23:02,267 --> 00:23:04,633
she will fight!

453
00:23:04,633 --> 00:23:09,233
They're going to regret
ever crossing her.

454
00:23:09,233 --> 00:23:12,100
And if she has no escape out,

455
00:23:12,100 --> 00:23:13,800
if she gets cornered,

456
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:16,567
someone will defend her.

457
00:23:17,467 --> 00:23:18,933
There will come...

458
00:23:20,367 --> 00:23:26,733
a knight in very shining armor.

459
00:23:26,767 --> 00:23:28,700
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

460
00:23:28,700 --> 00:23:29,767
Me.

461
00:23:29,767 --> 00:23:30,967
[LAUGHS]

462
00:23:31,967 --> 00:23:33,600
So bright it's blinding.

463
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:36,667
- I have work to do.
- Same here.

464
00:23:36,667 --> 00:23:37,733
[EXHALES LOUDLY]

465
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:46,633
[ENGINE REVVING]

466
00:23:46,633 --> 00:23:48,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

467
00:23:48,167 --> 00:23:50,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

468
00:23:50,133 --> 00:23:52,700
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECH]

469
00:23:53,333 --> 00:23:55,400
- [CAR HORNS HONKING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

470
00:23:57,500 --> 00:24:02,567
[PHONE BUZZING]

471
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:05,400
- Sam?
- Sir.

472
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:06,533
Suspicious character.

473
00:24:06,533 --> 00:24:08,000
I'm being followed.

474
00:24:09,500 --> 00:24:11,533
Four unidentified vehicles
are following me.

475
00:24:11,533 --> 00:24:12,533
Where are you right now?

476
00:24:12,533 --> 00:24:15,033
I'm approaching Soriano Street
near Reyes.

477
00:24:15,033 --> 00:24:17,633
When things go south,
I'll engage.

478
00:24:17,633 --> 00:24:19,433
I'll be sending agents
over there.

479
00:24:19,433 --> 00:24:21,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

480
00:24:21,033 --> 00:24:22,167
[TIRES SCREECHING]

481
00:24:22,167 --> 00:24:24,433
Make sure that woman
doesn't escape from us!

482
00:24:24,433 --> 00:24:27,933
[ENGINES REVVING]

483
00:24:27,933 --> 00:24:29,533
- Get close now!
- Copy that.

484
00:24:30,733 --> 00:24:34,867
[ENGINES REVVING]

485
00:24:34,867 --> 00:24:35,967
Drive faster!

486
00:24:35,967 --> 00:24:37,333
[TIRES SCREECH]

487
00:24:37,633 --> 00:24:40,433
Team, Agent Sam is
on Soriano Street.

488
00:24:40,433 --> 00:24:41,967
- She needs backup.
- Come on!

489
00:24:41,967 --> 00:24:43,033
Let's go!

490
00:24:43,633 --> 00:24:44,600
Thanks.

491
00:24:45,433 --> 00:24:46,667
Hey, wait a minute.

492
00:24:46,667 --> 00:24:47,867
Where are you going?

493
00:24:47,867 --> 00:24:50,800
Suspicious vehicles are
following Ma'am Sam.

494
00:24:50,800 --> 00:24:52,100
She needs backup.

495
00:24:52,100 --> 00:24:54,133
Someone might be planning
to do her harm,

496
00:24:54,133 --> 00:24:55,333
just like what happened
to Team Bravo.

497
00:24:55,333 --> 00:24:57,367
That can't be! Sam needs me!

498
00:24:57,367 --> 00:24:58,367
Let's move!

499
00:24:58,900 --> 00:25:01,100
[ENGINES REVVING]

500
00:25:01,100 --> 00:25:02,133
- [SCREAMS]
- [RAPID GUNFIRE]

501
00:25:02,167 --> 00:25:05,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

502
00:25:05,533 --> 00:25:08,400
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [ENGINES REVVING]

503
00:25:08,400 --> 00:25:11,133
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

504
00:25:12,333 --> 00:25:13,867
[GUNSHOTS]

505
00:25:17,900 --> 00:25:20,800
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

506
00:25:27,333 --> 00:25:29,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

507
00:25:29,233 --> 00:25:34,200
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

508
00:25:34,333 --> 00:25:35,400
[TIRES SCREECHING]

509
00:25:35,567 --> 00:25:36,700
[ENGINE REVVING]

510
00:25:39,067 --> 00:25:40,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

511
00:25:40,967 --> 00:25:46,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

512
00:25:46,967 --> 00:25:48,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

513
00:25:49,500 --> 00:25:50,833
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

514
00:25:50,967 --> 00:25:55,233
[GUNSHOTS]

515
00:25:55,367 --> 00:26:02,133
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

516
00:26:02,267 --> 00:26:06,300
[GUNSHOTS]

517
00:26:06,433 --> 00:26:13,167
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

518
00:26:20,533 --> 00:26:21,467
<i> I need results.</i>

519
00:26:21,667 --> 00:26:23,833
<i>We're wasting time and
money while my land sits idle.</i>

520
00:26:23,967 --> 00:26:25,333
<i>I've already spoken
to our connection.</i>

521
00:26:25,467 --> 00:26:26,967
<i>They're already working
on a way</i>

522
00:26:27,100 --> 00:26:28,533
<i>to push through
with the demolition.</i>

523
00:26:28,667 --> 00:26:30,833
<i>What if Gabo finds out
we're Django's men again?</i>

524
00:26:30,967 --> 00:26:33,033
<i>- Hey!
- What are you talking about?</i>

525
00:26:33,167 --> 00:26:35,733
<i>- Why?
- Ask these three traitors!</i>

526
00:26:35,867 --> 00:26:37,833
<i>They're back to working
with Django again.</i>

527
00:26:38,767 --> 00:26:40,033
<i> You know Mama's gone.</i>

528
00:26:40,167 --> 00:26:42,533
<i>You're the only important
person I have left now.</i>

529
00:26:42,700 --> 00:26:44,567
<i> I'm such a lucky father.</i>

530
00:26:44,700 --> 00:26:46,567
<i>I was blessed with a son
like you,</i>

531
00:26:46,700 --> 00:26:49,367
<i>and the woman you'll love
will be even luckier.</i>

532
00:26:49,600 --> 00:26:52,167
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

533
00:26:52,300 --> 00:26:53,467
<i> Let's split up!</i>

534
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:55,733
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

535
00:26:55,867 --> 00:26:57,133
<i> Get her!</i>

536
00:26:57,800 --> 00:26:59,367
<i> Don't let her get away!</i>

537
00:26:59,500 --> 00:27:01,633
<i>There's nowhere to run,
Jacinto!</i>

538
00:27:04,133 --> 00:27:06,767
<i>Whenever she has something
to do, she calls to let me know.</i>

539
00:27:06,900 --> 00:27:09,033
<i>She hasn't been in touch
since this morning,</i>

540
00:27:09,167 --> 00:27:11,567
<i>so I don't know
what happened to her.</i>

541
00:27:11,700 --> 00:27:14,067
<i>Better safe than sorry.
Open fire!</i>

542
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:15,767
[RAPID GUNFIRE]
